# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights in the portfolio project as requested.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` (v1.3.1) to project dependencies
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` accordingly

### 2. Component Integration
- Modified `src/App.tsx` to import and include the SpeedInsights component
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added the `<SpeedInsights />` component at the bottom of the App component, after the Footer
- This follows the React/Vite integration pattern from Vercel's documentation

## Implementation Details

The integration follows Vercel's official guidelines for React applications:
- Used `@vercel/speed-insights/react` package for seamless React integration
- Placed the component at the app root level for tracking across all pages
- The component is a wrapper around the tracking script that provides better React integration

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ No new linting errors introduced by the changes
✅ Package dependencies properly installed and lockfile updated
✅ Code follows existing project structure and conventions

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. The tracking script will be available at `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js`
3. Performance metrics will start appearing in the Speed Insights dashboard after visitors access the site

## Notes

- Pre-existing linting errors in the codebase (in ParticleBackground.tsx and UI components) were not addressed as they are unrelated to this implementation
- The SpeedInsights component will only send data when the app is deployed to Vercel's production environment
- No additional configuration is needed; the component works out of the box
